# effective-chain.rq — the LIVE chain of judgements for one region: the reading that was not
# superseded. Section repair adopts a pass-2 re-read of a band and links the two verdict
# decisions with dec:supersedes, so asking why-escalated.rq the obvious question about a
# repaired region returns the SUPERSEDED reading. This query follows that edge.
#
# Correct for both cases, so a consumer never needs to know which one they are in: if a
# superseding reading exists, its chain is returned; otherwise the region's own chain is.
# The FILTER NOT EXISTS is a HOLON-SCOPED closed-world guard (query-local, scoped to this one
# region, per CLAUDE.md §8) — it selects between two present readings, it never derives a
# fact from absence.
#
# ?region BINDING IS REQUIRED, not optional, and this is load-bearing: run with ?region
# unbound, branch B's FILTER NOT EXISTS is satisfied by ANY dec:supersedes edge anywhere in
# the graph (it is not scoped to a region until ?region is fixed), so the fallback branch
# vanishes for every region and the query silently returns only superseded-chain rows across
# the whole graph. Callers MUST pass ?region via initBindings (or an equivalent pre-bind);
# there is no way for the query itself to detect an unbound ?region and refuse.
#
# PRECONDITION: every dec:DecisionHolon that is the object of a dec:supersedes edge (a
# superseding verdict, ?v2) must carry dec:regarding. If one ever lacked it, branch A could
# not bind ?effective for that edge and branch B is excluded by the NOT EXISTS for the
# superseded region, so the query would return NOTHING for that region rather than falling
# back to the superseded chain. Unreachable today: decisionlog.py:52 (BandRecorder.record) emits
# dec:regarding on every judgement unconditionally.
#
# TRANSITIVE, NOT SINGLE-HOP (2026-09-14, R225 D2). This query used to follow exactly one
# dec:supersedes edge, which was safe only while a band could be superseded at most once per
# compile. D2's widened adoption gate lets a band that section repair has already re-read be
# adopted over by the page's data grid, and the maintainer's lineage ruling CHAINS those
# judgements (v1 <- v2 <- admission) rather than fanning them into one verdict. Following a
# single hop from ?v1 would now bind ?effective to v2's SECTION reading — a stale middle link
# returned as "effective", which is precisely what the comment this replaces predicted.
#
# ?vN IS THE HEAD OF THE CHAIN: it supersedes ?v1 transitively and nothing supersedes it. The
# FILTER NOT EXISTS is the same holon-scoped closed-world guard as branch B's (query-local,
# scoped to this region, CLAUDE.md §8) — it SELECTS among readings that are present and never
# derives a fact from absence. One hop is the special case where the head is the only
# superseder, so an unrepaired-then-adopted band answers exactly as it did before.
PREFIX dec: <https://w3id.org/iladub/dec#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
SELECT ?order ?judgement ?chosen ?rationale WHERE {
  {
    ?v1 dec:regarding ?region .
    ?vN dec:supersedes+ ?v1 ;
        dec:regarding ?effective .
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?later dec:supersedes ?vN }
  }
  UNION
  {
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?s dec:supersedes ?v . ?v dec:regarding ?region }
    BIND(?region AS ?effective)
  }
  ?d a dec:DecisionHolon ; dec:regarding ?effective ; dec:order ?order ;
     rdfs:label ?judgement ; dec:rationale ?rationale .
  OPTIONAL { ?d dec:chosen/rdfs:label ?chosen }
}
ORDER BY ?order
